#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:14
#: 6016e013421b473f861ede76fd4a1260
msgid "Chapter 22 — Cost, Privacy, Security"
msgstr "第 22 章 —— 成本、隐私、安全"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:16
#: 98e3300569c241a3b9d007fe245e6d50
msgid "Why"
msgstr "Why —— 为什么"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:18
#: 6cf8d9ea0e6c4a4f99bf19424728e4fb
msgid ""
"Every chapter up to this point has treated cost, privacy, and security as "
"constraints on individual decisions — use an embedding model whose pricing "
"makes re-embedding cheap (Chapter 10); keep L2's context bounded (Chapter "
"16); refuse to send `architecture/` to an LLM (Chapter 16's dispatcher). "
"These are the right local choices. But local good choices do not guarantee a"
" good global posture. A KB that would pass every chapter's individual rules "
"can still burn a team's LLM budget on noise, expose private content in "
"prompt logs, or publish a page whose content was written by an attacker."
msgstr ""
"到目前为止，每一章都把成本、隐私、安全当作对 * 局部 * 决策的约束 —— 选一款定价让“重新嵌入”变便宜的嵌入模型（第 10 章）；把 L2 "
"的上下文限制住（第 16 章）；拒绝把 `architecture/` 发给 LLM（第 16 "
"章的派发器）。这些都是正确的局部选择。但局部正确不等于全局姿态健康。一个每一章的规则都能单独通过的知识库，仍然可能把团队的 LLM "
"预算烧在噪声上、在提示词日志中泄露私密内容，或发布一个由攻击者写就的页面。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:28
#: 6e7893c1ddef4d4fa88daa77d37e8025
msgid ""
"This chapter consolidates the three constraints into operational disciplines"
" that bind across chapters. The centrepiece is the **token budget "
"discipline** — the cost discipline that the three-level update strategy "
"(Chapter 16) exists to support. Privacy and security complete the picture."
msgstr ""
"本章把这三条约束整合为贯通各章的运维纪律。核心是 **token 预算纪律** —— 第 16 章三级更新策略所支撑的成本纪律。隐私和安全补全这张图景。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:34
#: 85c3ea3421414bf3962d7f60e06ea335
msgid "What"
msgstr "What —— 是什么"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:36
#: fe9772e50fd342de9452a91693d8ca28
msgid "Three related questions, kept honest:"
msgstr "三个相互关联、都要诚实回答的问题："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:38
#: 1ed81833ece44226ad0116766b013a99
msgid ""
"**Cost.** *What does running this KB cost per commit, per sync, per year?* "
"Not the LLM-call-by-LLM-call question (which is trivial) but the aggregate "
"question (which is what a budget conversation requires)."
msgstr ""
"**成本。** * 运营这个知识库，按每次 commit、每次同步、每年来算要花多少钱？ * 不是“逐次 LLM 调用多少钱”那种琐碎问题，而是聚合成本"
" —— 这才是一次预算讨论真正要的答案。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:42
#: f0e5672549a7485e865bb2a401404db1
msgid ""
"**Privacy.** *What of our content leaves our walls, to whom, and under what "
"retention?* This is not a rhetorical question; it has concrete answers a KB "
"can enforce."
msgstr ""
"**隐私。** * 我们的哪些内容离开了我们的墙、发给了谁、按什么保留策略处置？ * "
"这不是一个修辞性问题；它有具体答案，而且知识库可以强制执行这些答案。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:45
#: 9ea1f58311b64bb8bee374f87d83631e
msgid ""
"**Security.** *Can a page's author be trusted? Can a page's content be "
"trusted? Can a page's citation be trusted?* These are distinct; each has its"
" own mechanism."
msgstr "**安全。** * 页面的作者可不可信？页面的内容可不可信？页面的引用可不可信？ * 三者各不相同；每一个都有自己的机制。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:49
#: 456e4ed8602041d7990ccdefa9b59ba6
msgid "How"
msgstr "How —— 怎么做"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:51
#: dce43cf43d964645afbbcb8f3f9b1c0a
msgid "The token budget discipline"
msgstr "Token 预算纪律"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:53
#: 1a6bff2cc77d49efa4cd00f1dbec3675
msgid ""
"The core move is this: **a KB's LLM cost should be a predictable function of"
" its commit rate, not its page count.** If the cost scales with pages, the "
"KB becomes more expensive as it gets more useful, which is the wrong "
"incentive. If it scales with commits, the KB's cost is proportional to the "
"project's actual change rate, which is exactly what a team is already "
"budgeting for."
msgstr ""
"核心那一步是这样说的： **一个知识库的 LLM 成本，应该是其 commit 频率的可预测函数，而不是页面数的可预测函数。** "
"如果成本随页面数扩，那么知识库越有用、就越贵 —— 这是错误的激励。如果成本随 commit 数扩，那么知识库的成本就与项目本身的变更率成正比 —— "
"而那本来就是团队已经在做预算的那个量。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:60
#: 8d6a4c905338401b97a791013ffc983f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This is one of the operational claims the author has refined in a private "
"project-knowledge-base toolkit {cite}`fanyamin_pkb_skill`: Chapter 16's "
"three-level update strategy exists precisely so commit cost stays bounded as"
" the KB grows. The arithmetic:"
msgstr ""
"这是作者在一个私有的 project-knowledge-base 工具包 {cite}`fanyamin_pkb_skill` "
"中反复打磨出的运维主张之一：第 16 章的三级更新策略存在的唯一目的，就是让 commit 成本在知识库增长时仍然保持有界。做一道算术题："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:65
#: 2171424281b7420f869128417a175c9a
msgid "**Naive baseline — \"regenerate every page whose topic changed\"**:"
msgstr "**朴素基线 —— “每一个话题发生变化的页面都重新生成”** ："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:67
#: 9d28f07cebf74b0981a5631b527ab215
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\text{cost}_\\text{naive} \\approx N_\\text{candidates} \\times C_\\text{full-page}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\text{cost}_\\text{naive} \\approx N_\\text{candidates} \\times C_\\text{full-page}\n"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:71
#: d161876edfa44628b07fe0e8c4fd583b
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where $N_\\text{candidates}$ grows with both the KB's size and the commit's "
"blast radius, and $C_\\text{full-page}$ is a full-page LLM call (~8–20 k "
"tokens for context plus the regenerated body)."
msgstr ""
"其中 $N_\\text{candidates}$ 会同时随“知识库规模”和“commit 的爆炸半径”一起增长， $C_\\text{full-"
"page}$ 则是一次整页 LLM 调用的成本（上下文加重新生成的正文，约 8–20 k tokens）。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:75
#: 30d435bb193e4c9fb2dd153eae85e333
msgid "**Three-level discipline — \"rule first, LLM second\"**:"
msgstr "**三级纪律 —— “rule first, LLM second”** ："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:77
#: 8dbec2282fad4141afa4f41a1de3debe
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\text{cost}_\\text{3L} \\approx N_\\text{L1} \\times 0 + N_\\text{L2} \\times C_\\text{bounded} + N_\\text{L3} \\times 0\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\text{cost}_\\text{3L} \\approx N_\\text{L1} \\times 0 + N_\\text{L2} \\times C_\\text{bounded} + N_\\text{L3} \\times 0\n"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:81
#: 94bcb47fa19f4532a0bf7660f6bedef1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where L1 and L3 spend zero LLM tokens (L1 is mechanical; L3 is human), and "
"$C_\\text{bounded}$ is a bounded call capped by Chapter 16 at ~5 k tokens. "
"Concretely, for the week of sync in Chapter 16's example (19 candidates, 12 "
"→ L1, 5 → L2, 2 → L3): five L2 calls at roughly 3 k tokens each. At 2024 "
"`text-embedding-3-small` / `gpt-4o-mini` pricing "
"{cite}`openai_embeddings_v3`, that is cents per week per repo. The naive "
"baseline on the same 19 candidates, at 15 k tokens each, is more than ten "
"times the spend *and* produces diffs that burn reviewer minutes — which, as "
"the previous chapter argued, is the costlier resource."
msgstr ""
"其中 L1 和 L3 花 0 个 LLM token（L1 是机械操作，L3 是人类操作）， $C_\\text{bounded}$ 是被第 16 "
"章上限在 ~5 k tokens 的有界调用。以第 16 章例子里那一周的同步为例（19 个候选，12 → L1、5 → L2、2 → L3）：五次 "
"L2 调用，每次约 3 k tokens。按 2024 年 `text-embedding-3-small` / `gpt-4o-mini` 的定价 "
"{cite}`openai_embeddings_v3` 来算，每个仓库每周就是几美分的事。朴素基线在同样 19 个候选上按每个 15 k tokens"
" 计，花费高出十倍以上， * 而且 * 会产出一堆 diff 去烧评审者的时间 —— 正如上一章所论，那才是更贵的资源。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:92
#: 7dba0de075034033b2deb1516900b274
msgid "The token budget discipline has three rules:"
msgstr "Token 预算纪律有三条规则："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:94
#: a537b122722b49fca4c42a9013c9dce3
msgid ""
"**Budget in commits, not pages.** Decide the cost-per-commit ceiling up "
"front (e.g. $\\$0.10 per commit for a small team; pennies for a well-tuned "
"pipeline). Track it. Alert on regression."
msgstr ""
"**以 commit 为单位做预算，而不是以页面为单位。** 事先定下“每次 commit 的成本上限”（比如小团队 "
"$\\$0.10/commit；调校良好的流水线只需几分钱）。追踪它。一旦回归就告警。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:97
#: 1a397b7ffb42495ab041c90bfac951e7
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**L1 ratio is a KPI.** The fraction of candidates handled by L1 is an "
"operational metric. An L1 ratio of 50% is healthy; 90% is excellent (and "
"usually means you have good auto-generated pages). An L1 ratio below 20% "
"means the rules are not capturing the common cases, or the KB is unnaturally"
" L2-heavy."
msgstr ""
"**L1 比例是一项 KPI。** “由 L1 处理的候选占比”是一个运维指标。50% 算健康；90% "
"算优秀（通常意味着你有一批好用的自动生成页）。L1 比例低于 20% 说明规则没有捕捉到常见场景，或者这个知识库“异常偏 L2”。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:102
#: 3221e8415b1348249a77284a8372310a
msgid ""
"**L3 is bounded by human attention, not token cost.** Do not attempt to "
"trade L3 for L2 to save dollars. The dollars were never the constraint."
msgstr "**L3 的约束是人的注意力，不是 token 成本。** 不要为了省钱就把本该 L3 的东西挪到 L2。钱从来不是约束。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:106
#: 60eb7710905e4f6082c18491015e5bb8
msgid ""
"These rules make the cost line on the dashboard a *leading indicator* of KB "
"health, not just an accounting number."
msgstr "这些规则让 dashboard 上的成本曲线成为知识库健康的 * 先行指标 * ，而不只是一个会计数字。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:109
#: e498211ad91445b197fbf4deca1f118e
msgid "Privacy: bounded context as a privacy property"
msgstr "隐私：把“有界上下文”视作一种隐私属性"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:111
#: 82919f7405eb47f4a8b3ce38c52199a0
msgid ""
"The L2 bounded-LLM strategy from Chapter 16 has a property the cost argument"
" does not exhaust: **bounded context is bounded disclosure.** Every time an "
"LLM is called, *some* content leaves the host. Depending on the provider, it"
" may be retained for model training, for abuse monitoring, or simply in "
"request logs. Even with a no-data-retention contract, prompts are held "
"transiently somewhere."
msgstr ""
"第 16 章那条 L2 有界 LLM 策略，还有一个成本论证未能穷尽的性质： **有界的上下文，等于有界的披露。** 每一次调用 LLM， * 总有一些"
" * 内容离开宿主。视供应方不同，这些内容可能被保留用于模型训练、滥用监控，或只是进了请求日志。即使签了“无数据保留”合同，提示词仍然会在某处短暂驻留。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:118
#: fd8513f3a712443e8f65df063088920c
msgid "The L2 discipline gives a direct privacy handle:"
msgstr "L2 纪律给了我们一个直接的隐私把手："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 74dafd63b806492ebeb66d077fd33c6e
msgid "Strategy"
msgstr "策略"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 4fdcce4e77304e2186a9822394728bd5
msgid "Sent per call"
msgstr "每次调用发送量"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 1750f629d04b4d16bc34d6a0d035a583
msgid "Annual disclosure surface"
msgstr "年度披露面"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: b85f150eb24e4849ac8f563ec5f1cf77
msgid "Naive full-regeneration"
msgstr "朴素的整页重生成"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: e446aa7eeba444ae97782f1a902b1d38
msgid "The whole page ~8–20 k tokens"
msgstr "整个页面，约 8–20 k tokens"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 71fb57e35f8846c3bbeb672ade22d86c
#, python-brace-format
msgid "≈ $N_\\text{pages} \\times$ weekly-regen-rate"
msgstr "≈ $N_\\text{pages} \\times$ 每周重生成率"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: d26b54d44da8466fbae8ab2bfba52f65
msgid "L2 bounded"
msgstr "L2 有界"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: a7b8696f44414799886b7dab0c4e9a15
msgid "One page's body + one diff ~2–5 k tokens"
msgstr "一个页面的正文 + 一份 diff，约 2–5 k tokens"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 3a3471d7d1fd4164b1a966737ad0839e
#, python-brace-format
msgid "≈ $N_\\text{L2-candidates}$ only"
msgstr "≈ 仅 $N_\\text{L2-candidates}$"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 19ff9b668f584a7caa3b3eb29079f5e3
msgid "L1 only"
msgstr "只走 L1"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: a0fa843ccb1b483b910c623c965a4aad
msgid "Nothing"
msgstr "什么都不发"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 5c08bcf688254db1a16033f461d2f4cf
msgid "None"
msgstr "无"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 333a46f0ae8b445680c74794b2f49a1e
msgid "L3 human-led"
msgstr "L3 人工主导"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: ce500c45348c4243aaafca61b89747f0
msgid "Whatever a human pastes"
msgstr "人粘贴什么就是什么"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md
#: 2107eeba1d724f3480cfecbbdfa16cf9
msgid "Human-controlled"
msgstr "由人来控制"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:127
#: 8d028fc4ac414d5baefb500f07128bb2
msgid ""
"L1's zero-disclosure property is the strongest privacy argument for \"rule "
"first, LLM second.\" Every rule that resolves a change at L1 is content that"
" never left the host. For KBs with sensitive content — security runbooks, "
"incident postmortems, internal architecture — the rule-first discipline is "
"not just a cost argument but a disclosure argument."
msgstr ""
"L1 的“零披露”性质是“rule first, LLM second”最有力的隐私论据。每一条在 L1 "
"消化掉变更的规则，对应着一段“从未离开宿主”的内容。对那些含有敏感内容的知识库 —— 安全 runbook、事故复盘、内部架构 —— 而言，rule-"
"first 纪律不只是成本论证，也是披露论证。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:134
#: 9aa03b6a5ab544c8af43c5e306610389
msgid "Three concrete actions follow:"
msgstr "由此可以落地三个具体动作："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:136
#: b082d3d8928a4d35bd1cec530174a8f1
msgid ""
"**Tag sensitive paths.** Paths like `security/`, `incidents/`, and `adr/` "
"(if ADRs discuss sensitive trade-offs) are tagged `privacy: restricted` in "
"the dispatcher config and are routed L3-only. The dispatcher rule is already"
" in Chapter 16; the privacy framing is *why* the rule exists."
msgstr ""
"**给敏感路径打标签。** `security/`、`incidents/`、以及 `adr/`（如果其中的 ADR "
"讨论敏感权衡）这样的路径，在派发器配置里被打上 `privacy: restricted`，只路由到 L3。派发器规则本身在第 16 "
"章已有；隐私视角说明的是 —— 这条规则 * 为什么 * 存在。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:141
#: 3b94f1aa3741456d9cd143be6a3258b1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Prefer self-hosted models for L2 on sensitive paths.** An open-weight "
"embedding and a small open LLM on local GPUs (e.g. the BGE family "
"{cite}`xiao2024bge`) can handle L2 for everything except the hardest L3 "
"escalations, at zero third-party disclosure."
msgstr ""
"**敏感路径上的 L2 优先使用自托管模型。** 本地 GPU 上跑一个开权重嵌入模型加一个小开源 LLM（例如 BGE 系列 "
"{cite}`xiao2024bge`）就足以承担 L2 的所有工作 —— 除去最难的那些本来就要升级到 L3 的情况 —— 而且对第三方的披露量为零。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:146
#: 77acd4c1508f438c8788e24ae4e9a0db
msgid ""
"**Log every L2 call.** Chapter 15's gate report can include a per-commit "
"ledger of which pages went to L2. This gives the team an auditable answer to"
" \"what did we send to the model provider this week?\" — which is both a "
"privacy control and a debugging aid."
msgstr ""
"**记录每一次 L2 调用。** 第 15 章的门禁报告可以附一份“每次 commit 有哪些页面走了 "
"L2”的账本。这让团队有一个可审计的答案来回应“这一周我们到底向模型供应商发了什么？” —— 它既是一条隐私控制，也是调试工具。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:152
#: b2daf27b545747969425409e2099de62
msgid "Security: three independent trust questions"
msgstr "安全：三个互相独立的信任问题"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:154
#: 7252029d36a5474f8d2020e58fcd3614
msgid ""
"Security of a KB is not a single question. Three distinct questions, each "
"with its own mechanism:"
msgstr "知识库的安全性不是单一问题。它是三个各有其机制的独立问题："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:157
#: f4c840889b274c35a353625be9f0dfbb
msgid ""
"**Can the author be trusted?** Mechanism: `created_by` + `updated_by` fields"
" (Chapter 5), enforced by `MergeFrontmatterUpdate`'s immutability rule. A "
"page never loses its origin authorship. The Git history provides a second, "
"independent record."
msgstr ""
"**作者可不可信？** 机制：`created_by` + `updated_by` 字段（第 5 章），由 "
"`MergeFrontmatterUpdate` 的不可变性规则强制执行。一个页面永远不会丢失它最初的作者身份。Git 历史提供了第二份独立记录。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:162
#: f6e6d66191e84b99acd44ee6a5588c07
msgid ""
"**Can the content be trusted?** Mechanism: the footer's `review_status` + "
"`review_score` (Chapter 5), the hard gates (Chapter 15 H3), and the AI-"
"always-sets-pending rule. A page whose content has been touched but not "
"reviewed is `review_status: pending` — explicitly."
msgstr ""
"**内容可不可信？** 机制：footer 里的 `review_status` + `review_score`（第 5 章）、硬门禁（第 15 章 "
"H3），以及“AI 总是置 pending”规则。一个内容被动过、但尚未被评审的页面是 `review_status: pending` —— "
"显式为之。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:167
#: d9a6df8763cd4332a78918ab6b4787e6
msgid ""
"**Can the citations be trusted?** Mechanism: H4 in Chapter 15 every "
"`file:line` anchor resolves at HEAD. An adversarial or hallucinated citation"
" fails the gate and blocks publish."
msgstr ""
"**引用可不可信？** 机制：第 15 章的 H4 —— 每一个 `file:line` 锚点都必须在 HEAD "
"处解析成功。任何对抗性的或幻觉出来的引用都会通不过门禁，从而阻止发布。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:171
#: f1ba7fd01dcc41a2be534769d9af185b
msgid ""
"Attacks on a KB tend to split along the same three axes. Authorship attacks "
"are Git-level (compromised account, rogue PR); content-drift attacks are "
"stale-page attacks (something true once is no longer true, an attacker "
"exploits the belief it is); citation attacks are the most pernicious "
"category — a page that claims to cite the code but does not — and these are "
"also the most mechanically defensible because citation resolution is "
"decidable."
msgstr ""
"针对知识库的攻击也倾向于沿同样的三条轴分裂。作者攻击发生在 Git 层面（账号被盗、恶意 "
"PR）；内容漂移攻击是“陈旧页面”攻击（从前为真的某件事如今不再为真，攻击者利用“人们仍相信它为真”这一点）；引用攻击则是其中最恶毒的一类 —— "
"页面声称自己引用了代码、实则没有 —— 而它们恰恰是最容易用机械手段防御的，因为“引用能不能解析”是可判定的。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:179
#: cd712e8a0ce443c283155f20139fec4c
msgid "The three-layer threat model"
msgstr "三层威胁模型"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:181
#: 59179262e27346eb90d5e187c3fe1ce0
msgid ""
"Putting it together, a page in a well-run KB carries three independent "
"attestations:"
msgstr "把它们放在一起看：一个运作良好的知识库中的页面，背后有三份互相独立的证明："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:190
#: 0ef413a5374947bdb8b998e006fda8a3
msgid ""
"An attacker must compromise all three layers to plant a page that looks "
"legitimate. Compromising Git is hard if the team uses signed commits; "
"compromising the review requires the reviewer's signature in the footer; "
"compromising citations is almost impossible because the citations are "
"checked mechanically at publish time. Each layer is independently cheap; "
"together they are considerably stronger than any single layer."
msgstr ""
"攻击者必须同时攻破这三层，才能种下一个“看起来合法”的页面。如果团队使用签名 commit，攻破 Git 就很难；攻破评审要伪造评审者在 footer "
"中的签名；攻破引用则几乎不可能，因为引用在发布时是被机械式校验的。每一层单独代价都很低；三层叠加起来，比任何单层都要强得多。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:198
#: 24bb35c65ea64e028621062f8e5f613b
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Example —— 范例"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:200
#: c5afe31e390246abb895d83b58f9c9ab
msgid ""
"A concrete budget-and-disclosure sheet for one mid-sized KB (numbers "
"anonymised but operationally realistic):"
msgstr "一份针对某中型知识库的具体“预算与披露表”（数据已匿名化，但运维上真实合理）："

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:227
#: 0d023b1c33e247ebbf345d7f9bfbcc87
msgid ""
"Every line is a rule or a mechanism explained in one of the earlier "
"chapters. This chapter's contribution is putting them on a single page so "
"the governance conversation has something concrete to look at."
msgstr "每一行都对应之前某一章讲过的某条规则或某个机制。本章的贡献是把它们集中到同一张纸上，让“治理对话”在桌面上有个实实在在可看的东西。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:232
#: c4e8d41f86304c41b120c96125481bd4
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "Conclusion —— 小结"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:234
#: 0ef2cc74b7484f55ad47b39f54f87c55
msgid ""
"Cost, privacy, and security are usually treated as three separate concerns. "
"Run through the operational model of Chapter 7a, they turn out to share a "
"common spine: the three-level update strategy bounds tokens (cost), bounds "
"disclosure (privacy), and leaves the hardest cases to a human (security). "
"None of that machinery is new in this chapter. What is new is the claim that"
" *these three properties are the same property* — the discipline of not "
"letting an LLM touch what a rule or a human can touch better, cheaper, and "
"more privately."
msgstr ""
"成本、隐私、安全通常被当作三件独立的关切。但把它们放到第 7 章 a 节的运维模型里走一遍，就会发现它们其实共享同一条主脊：三级更新策略把 token "
"界住（成本）、把披露界住（隐私）、并把最棘手的情形留给人（安全）。本章提到的机制没有一条是新的；新的是这个主张 —— * 这三个性质其实是同一个性质 *"
" ：不让 LLM 去碰那些“规则或人能够更好、更便宜、更私密地处理”的东西，这条纪律本身。"

#: ../../part6-governance-and-outlook/ch22-cost-privacy-security.md:243
#: 923ac1cacdb84551a6055517bf010eb5
msgid ""
"The next chapter discusses trust and red-teaming: once the operational model"
" is in place, how does a KB actually get tested against adversarial use?"
msgstr "下一章讨论信任与红队演练：一旦运维模型就位，一个知识库到底如何在对抗性使用下被测试？"

